{"toolCallId":"call_881da51f283145a09fe4a5e7b2e8b63a","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"58-| `ANCHORS_VALID`      | ERROR    | spec docs with anchored templates | Anchors present, paired and not nested (adr-NNN may hold adr-NNN-*) |\n59-| `FOLDER_NAMING`      | ERROR    | Folder path   | Folder follows ###-short-name convention       |\n60-| `FRONTMATTER_VALID`  | ERROR    | spec docs     | YAML frontmatter properly structured           |\n61:| `COMPLEXITY_MATCH`   | WARNING  | All levels    | Content metrics match declared level           |\n62-| `AI_PROTOCOLS`       | ERROR    | Level 3/3+    | AI execution protocols present                 |\n63-| `LEVEL_MATCH`        | ERROR    | All files     | Level consistent across all spec files         |\n64-| `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY` | ERROR  | spec docs, goal.md | Anchor sufficiency; for `goal.md` also the durable budget (one limit: fail past 4000) and binding-row existence |\n65-| `FRONTMATTER_VALUES` | WARNING  | packet docs   | `contextType` or `importance_tier` outside sk-create-frontmatter's `frontmatter-values.json`; aliases are legal |\n66-| `SOURCE_TAGS`        | WARNING  | research/ + review/ | `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags that name a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, in packets created after the cutoff |\n67-\n68-> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set and their canonical severities live in [`runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json).\n69-\n70-### AC_CLOSURE\n71-\n72-`AC_CLOSURE` decides whether a packet may be closed. It is registered at ERROR severity and runs by default; set `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=false` to opt out.\n73-\n74-**Rule ID:** `AC_CLOSURE`\n75-\n76-**Scope:** Levels 2, 3 and 3+. Level 1 keeps acceptance criteria inline in `spec.md` and is never gated.\n77-\n78-**Rollout:** forward-only behind `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF` (default `2026-08-30`), compared against the `Created` date in the packet's `spec.md` metadata table. A packet created on or before the cutoff, or whose date cannot be read, is advisory on **every** branch — presence, waiver integrity and completion alike — and is never blocked. A malformed override falls back to the default rather than being compared as a string, which would otherwise grandfather the whole repository. This mirrors the `CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF` pattern rather than introducing a third grandfathering mechanism.\n79-\n80-**Failure modes:**\n81-\n82-| Condition | Result |\n83-|---|---|\n84-| Post-cutoff packet with no `acceptance-criteria.md` | `fail` — the document is required at these levels |\n85-| A row marked `Waived` or `Superseded` naming no ADR | `fail` — an unbacked waiver is not a pass |\n86-| A criterion row that cannot be parsed, or an unbalanced code fence | `fail` — a dropped row would empty the table and close the packet |\n--\n593-\n594----\n595-\n596:## 9. COMPLEXITY_MATCH\n597-\n598-**Severity:** WARNING\n599-**Description:** Validates that declared complexity level matches actual content metrics (user stories, phases, tasks).\n600-\n601-### Expected Ranges by Level\n602-\n603-| Level | User Stories | Phases  | Tasks     |\n604-| ----- | ------------ | ------- | --------- |\n605-| 1     | 1-2          | 2-3     | 5-15      |\n606-| 2     | 2-4          | 3-5     | 15-50     |\n607-| 3/3+  | 4-15         | 5-12    | 50-200    |\n608-\n609-### Detection Patterns\n610-\n611-| Metric       | Pattern Searched                           |\n612-| ------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n613-| User Stories | `### User Story` headers in spec.md        |\n614-| Phases       | `### Phase` headers in plan.md             |\n615-| Tasks        | `- [ ] T##` or `- [ ] TASK-` in tasks.md   |\n616-\n617-### Examples\n618-\n619-**Warning (under-scoped for Level 2):**\n620-```\n621-Declared Level: 2\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"22ddf0","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_8be416bdcd2a4e6db2d40d3264fc0557","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"64:| `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY` | ERROR  | spec docs, goal.md | Anchor sufficiency; for `goal.md` also the durable budget (one limit: fail past 4000) and binding-row existence |\n65-| `FRONTMATTER_VALUES` | WARNING  | packet docs   | `contextType` or `importance_tier` outside sk-create-frontmatter's `frontmatter-values.json`; aliases are legal |\n66-| `SOURCE_TAGS`        | WARNING  | research/ + review/ | `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags that name a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, in packets created after the cutoff |\n67-\n68-> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set and their canonical severities live in [`runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json).\n69-\n70-### AC_CLOSURE\n71-\n72-`AC_CLOSURE` decides whether a packet may be closed. It is registered at ERROR severity and runs by default; set `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=false` to opt out.\n73-\n74-**Rule ID:** `AC_CLOSURE`\n75-\n76-**Scope:** Levels 2, 3 and 3+. Level 1 keeps acceptance criteria inline in `spec.md` and is never gated.\n77-\n78-**Rollout:** forward-only behind `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF` (default `2026-08-30`), compared against the `Created` date in the packet's `spec.md` metadata table. A packet created on or before the cutoff, or whose date cannot be read, is advisory on **every** branch — presence, waiver integrity and completion alike — and is never blocked. A malformed override falls back to the default rather than being compared as a string, which would otherwise grandfather the whole repository. This mirrors the `CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF` pattern rather than introducing a third grandfathering mechanism.\n79-\n80-**Failure modes:**\n81-\n82-| Condition | Result |\n83-|---|---|\n84-| Post-cutoff packet with no `acceptance-criteria.md` | `fail` — the document is required at these levels |\n--\n766:**Rule:** `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY`, diagnostics `SPECDOC_SUFFICIENCY_005` (budget) and `SPECDOC_SUFFICIENCY_006` (binding)  \n767-**Description:** A packet `goal.md` carries the directive an operator sets as the session objective. Every runtime goal surface caps what it holds and truncates at the tail, where the completion criteria live, so the slice that gets set has a budget.\n768-\n769-### What Is Measured\n770-\n771-The durable slice: everything after the frontmatter's closing `---` up to `<!-- ANCHOR:log -->`, anchors and comments included, counted in characters. The frontmatter is never part of it and never leaves the file. The log is volatile and never part of it.\n772-\n773-### Where It Applies\n774-\n775-- **Phase parents** and **top-level packets**: one limit of 4,000 characters. Up to 4,000 passes with no diagnostic; past it fails. These are the documents an operator sets. A folder that resolves to the phase level counts as a phase parent even when it sits inside another packet.\n776-- **Phase children** that are not themselves phase parents: unbounded. A child binds through its parent and is never set directly.\n777-\n778-The goal command and `check-goal.cjs` draw the same line. Section 2 of sk-create-goal's [budget-and-handoff.md](../../../sk-doc/sk-create-goal/references/budget-and-handoff.md) states it for goal authors.\n779-\n780-The limit lives in `templates/spec-kit-docs.json` as `goalDurableBudget.errorChars`, which the validator and the goal command read, and which the template and this reference quote.\n781-\n782-### Binding Rows\n783-\n784-On a phase parent the `binding` anchor lists each child's goal document. Every row's path must exist on disk. A row naming a child `goal.md` that was never authored is an error: the parent promises a directive the child cannot supply.\n785-\n786-### Examples\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"b87130","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
